<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polish–Lithuanian–Teutonic War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1409">1409</a>–<a href="/years/1411">1411</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Great War (1409–1411)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Polish–Lithuanian–Teutonic War was fought from 1409 to 1411 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Knights</a> and the allied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>. Its decisive event, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-grunwald">Battle of Grunwald</a> in 1410, broke the order's military power, though its castle of Marienburg held out; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-peace-of-thorn">First Peace of Thorn</a> (1411) returned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samogitia">Samogitia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> for the lifetimes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o">Jogaila</a> and Vytautas.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-teutonic-war.jpg" alt="Polish–Lithuanian–Teutonic War" width="320" height="143" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Matejko · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jan_Matejko,_Bitwa_pod_Grunwaldem.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
